{
  "Hi, I'm Vamshi Kanderao.": "933ab3c0228b.m4a",
  "Déjà Vu isn't a chatbot. It's a memory layer any personal agent can add,": "b9ee75484155.m4a",
  "Muse, ChatGPT, Claude, or your own.": "fddcd7e03a5d.m4a",
  "It learns from your chats, checks when it matters, and runs on Meta's Muse models.": "0ea25f5b18fe.m4a",
  "Here's the issue. Your agent remembers you, but never checks if it's still true.": "6e89c9ef457b.m4a",
  "You can't see what it guessed, or why.": "9e32882fb95b.m4a",
  "So an old assumption either gets buried,": "420819a89352.m4a",
  "or gets too expensive to reach the agent.": "b3b1eaee7342.m4a",
  "Déjà Vu flips it: it runs on what you confirm.": "1405a4783220.m4a",
  "Every card shows its source.": "3720274fc4cc.m4a",
  "It asks once, only when it matters most.": "5051f9a51e8b.m4a",
  "And it reads short cards, not a summary.": "79cf344e7644.m4a",
  "No setup: just drop in your chat export.": "271c97c03ff8.m4a",
  "Let's watch a live demo.": "5d1f14764a3b.m4a",
  "The chat is just a host. Déjà Vu is the memory inside it.": "8e60f9f1ad06.m4a",
  "The eval: fourteen people, three hundred and twelve checks.": "25d4aab3978d.m4a",
  "Déjà Vu got eighty percent right. A summary, seventy-two.": "b19e061ca480.m4a",
  "When a preference changed and was never mentioned: eighty-one percent. The others, about half.": "8bc718aebf8d.m4a",
  "And ninety-four percent fewer tokens than re-reading the history.": "9e4c7504256e.m4a",
  "Agents will keep getting better at guessing who you are.": "493a0f0ff662.m4a",
  "But a guess is still a guess. Confirmed memory beats inferred memory.": "c0d31e7fa5b8.m4a",
  "Next time an agent says it knows you, ask it to show you. Thank you.": "b87544779ddd.m4a",
  "Under the hood: Muse Spark writes the cards, Muse Wonder grades each one, memory stays bounded, and any agent plugs in over HTTP.": "0746159689c5.m4a",
  "handback": "d8868f58b49b.m4a"
}
